.Dd June 5, 2026
.Dt MAC_CAPABILITY_ACCOUNTING 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mac_capability_accounting
.Nd MAC_CAPABILITY per-process resource accounting and enforcement
.Sh SYNOPSIS
To load at boot:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
echo 'mac_capability_accounting_load="YES"' >> /boot/loader.conf
.Ed
.Pp
Wire protocol header:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
#include <dev/mac_capability/mac_capability_accounting_proto.h>
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
service provides per-process
.Xr racct 4
resource accounting and
.Xr rctl 8
enforcement rule management via
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_CALL .
The service is registered under the name
.Dq accounting .
.Pp
Connection requires
.Dv PRIV_ACCT
privilege.
The target process is identified by attaching a
.Xr procdesc 4
file descriptor to the call.
If no fd is attached, the operation targets the caller.
.Ss Operations
.Bl -tag -width "ACCT_OP_REMOVE_RULE"
.It Dv ACCT_OP_CHARGE Pq 1
Debit a resource amount via
.Fn racct_add .
.It Dv ACCT_OP_RELEASE Pq 2
Credit a resource amount via
.Fn racct_sub .
.It Dv ACCT_OP_SET Pq 3
Set a resource to an absolute value via
.Fn racct_set .
.It Dv ACCT_OP_ADD_RULE Pq 4
Add an
.Xr rctl 8
enforcement rule.
.It Dv ACCT_OP_REMOVE_RULE Pq 5
Remove an
.Xr rctl 8
enforcement rule.
.It Dv ACCT_OP_GET_RULES Pq 6
Query the active enforcement rules for the target process.
.El
.Ss Wire Structures
Charge, release, and set operations use:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
struct acct_charge_request {
	uint32_t  op;        /* ACCT_OP_CHARGE/RELEASE/SET */
	uint32_t  resource;  /* RACCT_* constant */
	uint64_t  amount;
} __packed;
.Ed
.Pp
Rule operations use:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
struct acct_rule_request {
	uint32_t  op;        /* ACCT_OP_ADD_RULE/REMOVE_RULE */
	uint32_t  resource;  /* RACCT_* constant */
	uint32_t  action;    /* ACCT_RULE_* */
	uint32_t  signal;    /* signal number if ACCT_RULE_SIGNAL */
	uint64_t  limit;     /* trigger threshold */
} __packed;
.Ed
.Pp
The get-rules request uses:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
struct acct_get_rules_request {
	uint32_t  op;        /* ACCT_OP_GET_RULES */
	uint32_t  _reserved;
} __packed;
.Ed
.Pp
The reply for charge, release, set, add-rule, and remove-rule:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
struct acct_reply {
	uint32_t  status;
	uint32_t  _pad;
} __packed;
.Ed
.Pp
The reply for get-rules:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
#define ACCT_MAX_RULES  16

struct acct_rule_entry {
	uint32_t  resource;
	uint32_t  action;
	uint32_t  signal;
	uint32_t  _pad;
	uint64_t  limit;
} __packed;

struct acct_rules_reply {
	uint32_t               status;
	uint32_t               nrules;
	struct acct_rule_entry rules[ACCT_MAX_RULES];
} __packed;
.Ed
.Ss Rule Actions
.Bl -column "Dv ACCT_RULE_THROTTLE" "Value" "send signal" -offset indent
.It Sy Constant Ta Sy Value Ta Sy Description
.It Dv ACCT_RULE_DENY Ta 1 Ta fail allocation
.It Dv ACCT_RULE_LOG Ta 2 Ta log violation
.It Dv ACCT_RULE_THROTTLE Ta 3 Ta sleep process
.It Dv ACCT_RULE_SIGNAL Ta 4 Ta send signal
.El
.Pp
When
.Fa action
is
.Dv ACCT_RULE_SIGNAL ,
the
.Fa signal
field specifies the signal number (1 through
.Dv _SIG_MAXSIG ) .
.Ss Status Codes
.Bl -column "Dv ACCT_STATUS_DENIED" "Value" -offset indent
.It Sy Constant Ta Sy Value
.It Dv ACCT_STATUS_OK Ta 0
.It Dv ACCT_STATUS_ERR Ta 1
.It Dv ACCT_STATUS_DEAD Ta 2
.It Dv ACCT_STATUS_DENIED Ta 3
.It Dv ACCT_STATUS_EPERM Ta 4
.El
.Pp
.Dv ACCT_STATUS_DEAD
is returned when the target process has exited.
.Dv ACCT_STATUS_DENIED
is returned when a charge or set operation would exceed a resource limit.
If the kernel is compiled without
.Dv RACCT
or
.Dv RCTL
support, the corresponding operations return
.Dv ACCT_STATUS_ERR .
.Sh DTRACE PROBES
The following DTrace probes are provided under the
.Nm mac_capability_acct
provider:
.Bl -tag -width "state"
.It Cm state Ns Pq Ar op, resource, amount, status, pid, error
Fires on completion of charge, release, set, rule-add, and rule-remove
operations.
.It Cm deny Ns Pq Ar reason, uid, error
Fires when an operation is denied, including connection attempts
without
.Dv PRIV_ACCT
and racct limit violations.
.El
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EINVAL
Request too small, reply buffer too small, invalid resource constant,
invalid operation code, or invalid signal number for
.Dv ACCT_RULE_SIGNAL .
.It Bq Er EPERM
The caller lacks
.Dv PRIV_ACCT
privilege (connection refused).
.It Bq Er ESRCH
The attached procdesc does not reference a valid process.
.El
.Pp
Application-level errors are returned in the
.Fa status
field of the reply structure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mac_capability 4 ,
.Xr procdesc 4 ,
.Xr authorityd 8 ,
.Xr rctl 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
first appeared in 5BSD.
